      "note": "both level-B items come from one LACE-Bio pooled analysis of four adjuvant cisplatin trials (EIDs 1148 and 1149; PMID 26899019). The paper is more careful than the pair of items suggests: TP53 mutation was \"marginally predictive\" of benefit from adjuvant chemotherapy (interaction p = 0.06 for overall survival), with wild-type disease showing a tendency toward better outcomes on chemotherapy than on observation (HR 0.77, 95% CI 0.62-0.95) and mutant disease showing none. Either way the selection is of chemotherapy on TP53 status; nothing is aimed at TP53, which is what its target card says"
